    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n9 Sallynoggin Road Lower is a charming mid-terraced cottage extending to approximately 50.9 sq.m. (548 sq.ft.). Well maintained throughout, this appealing home offers a practical and comfortable layout, ideally suited to first-time buyers, downsizers or investors seeking a property in a highly convenient location. The property also offers plenty of scope to further enhance and modernise the accommodation, with several key upgrades already completed, including upgraded double-glazed windows, a new front door and a refurbished bathroom.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hall, living room, bedroom and inner hall leading to a study with extensive fitted wardrobes. To the rear of the property are the kitchen and bathroom, together with access to a private northwest-facing patio. Compact yet practical in design, the layout maximises the available space and provides a solid canvas for a purchaser wishing to update and personalise the property over time.\n\nOutside, the rear patio enjoys a northwest orientation and provides a private, low-maintenance outdoor space, ideal for relaxing or outdoor dining.\nSituated in the heart of Sallynoggin, No. 9 enjoys an exceptionally convenient location with a wealth of amenities on its doorstep. Local shops, schools, cafés and supermarkets are all within walking distance, while nearby Dún Laoghaire, Monkstown and Glasthule offer an excellent range of restaurants, leisure facilities and coastal attractions. The area is well served by Dublin Bus routes and nearby DART stations, making commuting to the city centre both quick and convenient."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nlaminate flooring, centre light\n\nLiving Room: - 3.31m x 4.20m\nfireplace with marble hearth, centre light, window overlooking the front\n\nBedroom 1: - 3.02m x 3.35m\ncentre light, wall shelving, hot press, GFCH boiler, original fireplace, window overlooking the front\n\nInner Hall: - \nglass panel doors, centre light\n\nStudy - 3.31m x 2.53m\ndouble room, extensive floor-to-ceiling sliding wardrobes, recessed shelving, centre light, Velux roof window, original fireplace\n\nKitchen: - 2.86m x 3.67m max\nwall and floor mounted kitchen units, Beko gas hob and grill, Beko washer/dryer, stainless steel sink unit, window overlooking the courtyard\n\nBathroom: - 1.30m x 3.67m\ntiled flooring, partly tiled walls, WC, wash hand basin inset in vanity unit, Mira shower with glass screen\n\nRear Courtyard: - \nnorthwest-facing courtyard with artificial grass and trellis fencing\n\n"
      },
